Superposition of SHM

When two or more Simple Harmonic Waves coincide parallel to each other, 
they "superimpose" on eachother to form a resultant wave, with a resultant amplitude.

y1 = A1sin(wt)
y2 = A2sin(wt + P)

y_res= y1 + y2;

where P is the phase difference,
resultant amplitude A_Res = sqr(A1) + sqr(A2) + 2 x A1 x A2 x cosP
